# DianaSh golden corpus. Recorded from the C# shell, byte for byte; EMUSEN_DIANASH_GOLDEN=record rewrites it - see EmuSen_DianaSh.md §13.4.
# Patterns: <ROOT> is the sandbox's real root, <TEMP> the corpus's real temporary folder, <INSTALL> the install's real directory;
# a 'match' block is a regular expression the whole output must match, written where a line prints a time or a measured number.
command memcard
usage 1   memcard ls [<card>]           every card under Saves, or the saves on one card
usage 2   memcard cp <card>:<save> <card>
usage 3                                 copy a save onto another card of its medium
usage 4   memcard mv <card>:<save> <card>
usage 5                                 copy a save, read it back, then delete the first
usage 6   memcard rm <card>:<save>      delete a save as the console's own manager does
usage 7   memcard import <card> <from>...
usage 8                                 every save of <from> onto <card>, all or none
usage 9   memcard new <card>            a new card, formatted where its medium allows
usage 10   memcard dup <card> <new>      a whole card copied to a new name
usage 11   memcard rename <card> <new>   a card renamed

case the cards of every console, and new ones
target none
covers 1,9
$ memcard ls
out 72
No cards: nothing under Saves is a file of a medium a system pack names.
status 0
action none
$ memcard new Saves/PlayStation/Cards/Blue.mcr
out 38
Blue.mcr made, a formatted memory card
status 0
action none
$ memcard ls
out 92
PlayStation
  Saves/PlayStation/Cards/Blue.mcr  Memory Card  0 save(s), 15 of 15 blocks free
status 0
action none
$ memcard ls Saves/PlayStation/Cards/Blue.mcr
out 78
Saves/PlayStation/Cards/Blue.mcr  Memory Card  0 save(s), 15 of 15 blocks free
status 0
action none
$ memcard new Saves/PlayStation/Cards/Blue.mcr
out 32
memcard: Blue.mcr already exists
status 1
action none
$ memcard new "Saves/Sega CD/Cards/Cartridge 1.crm"
out 54
Cartridge 1.crm made, a formatted backup RAM cartridge
status 0
action none
end

case copy, move, delete and import on cards with no saves
target none
covers 2-8
$ memcard new Saves/PlayStation/Cards/Blue.mcr
out 38
Blue.mcr made, a formatted memory card
status 0
action none
$ memcard new Saves/PlayStation/Cards/Red.mcr
out 37
Red.mcr made, a formatted memory card
status 0
action none
$ memcard cp Saves/PlayStation/Cards/Blue.mcr:1 Saves/PlayStation/Cards/Red.mcr
out 33
memcard: no save 1 is on Blue.mcr
status 1
action none
$ memcard mv Saves/PlayStation/Cards/Blue.mcr:BASLUS-00067 Saves/PlayStation/Cards/Red.mcr
out 44
memcard: no save BASLUS-00067 is on Blue.mcr
status 1
action none
$ memcard rm Saves/PlayStation/Cards/Blue.mcr
out 130
memcard: 'Saves/PlayStation/Cards/Blue.mcr' names no save; write <card>:<save>, the save by its name or its number in 'memcard ls'
status 1
action none
$ memcard rm Saves/PlayStation/Cards/Blue.mcr:1
out 33
memcard: no save 1 is on Blue.mcr
status 1
action none
$ memcard import Saves/PlayStation/Cards/Red.mcr Saves/PlayStation/Cards/Blue.mcr
out 44
0 save(s), 0 block(s), imported onto Red.mcr
status 0
action none
end

case a whole card duplicated and renamed
target none
covers 9-11
$ memcard new Saves/PlayStation/Cards/Blue.mcr
out 38
Blue.mcr made, a formatted memory card
status 0
action none
$ memcard dup Saves/PlayStation/Cards/Blue.mcr Saves/PlayStation/Cards/Green.mcr
out 34
Blue.mcr copied whole to Green.mcr
status 0
action none
$ memcard dup Saves/PlayStation/Cards/Blue.mcr Saves/PlayStation/Cards/Green.mcr
out 65
memcard: Green.mcr already exists; nothing is written over a card
status 1
action none
$ memcard rename Saves/PlayStation/Cards/Green.mcr Saves/PlayStation/Cards/Teal.mcr
out 26
Green.mcr renamed Teal.mcr
status 0
action none
$ memcard ls
out 173
PlayStation
  Saves/PlayStation/Cards/Blue.mcr  Memory Card  0 save(s), 15 of 15 blocks free
  Saves/PlayStation/Cards/Teal.mcr  Memory Card  0 save(s), 15 of 15 blocks free
status 0
action none
end

case what it refuses
target none
covers 1
$ memcard
out 72
Usage: memcard ls|cp|mv|rm|import|new|dup|rename ... (see 'man memcard')
status 1
action none
$ memcard frob
out 72
Usage: memcard ls|cp|mv|rm|import|new|dup|rename ... (see 'man memcard')
status 1
action none
$ memcard ls /../x.mcr
out 60
memcard: '/../x.mcr' is outside the project sandbox (<ROOT>)
status 1
action none
$ memcard ls notes.txt
out 175
memcard: notes.txt is no card: the media known are .crm (Backup RAM Cartridge), .brm (Internal Backup RAM), .mcr (Memory Card), .mpk (Controller Pak), .ps2 (Memory Card (PS2))
status 1
action none
$ memcard cp notes.txt Saves/PlayStation/Cards/Blue.mcr
out 107
memcard: 'notes.txt' names no save; write <card>:<save>, the save by its name or its number in 'memcard ls'
status 1
action none
end
